{meta title='A PHP crossword', about='Ten words about PHP laid out on the server - the empty grid to print, with the clues beside it.'}
{crossword title='PHP crossword'}
  ARRAY: An ordered map, the workhorse of PHP
  ECHO: A language construct that outputs one or more strings
  CLOSURE: An anonymous function that captures variables with use
  COMPOSER: The dependency manager most projects install
  ENUM: A type with a fixed set of cases, new in 8.1
  NULL: The value of a variable that has none
  MATCH: The stricter switch, an expression since 8.0
  YIELD: Hands a value out of a generator and pauses it
  LARAVEL: A framework with Eloquent and Blade
  STATIC: Late binding keyword, or a property of the class
{/crossword}
